  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": null,
      "gridPos": { "h": 22, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "id": 200,
      "options": {
        "code": { "language": "plaintext", "showLineNumbers": false, "showMiniMap": false },
        "content": "## Integrate a project into this observability stack\n\nCopy the prompt below and give it to your AI agent:\n\n```\nYou are integrating a Docker Compose project into a shared observability stack.\n\nThe observability stack is already running on this host. Your job is to connect\nthis project to it by making the following changes to its docker-compose.yml:\n\n1. Declare the external observability network at the bottom of the file:\n\n   networks:\n     observability:\n       name: observability\n       external: true\n\n2. For every service that should be observed, add the observability network\n   and these labels (replace values as appropriate):\n\n   labels:\n     obs.service.name: \"<service-name>\"        # e.g. \"api\", \"worker\", \"frontend\"\n     obs.service.namespace: \"<project-name>\"   # e.g. \"my-app\" — groups services in dashboards\n\n   networks:\n     - <existing-network>   # keep whatever networks the service already uses\n     - observability\n\n3. If a service exposes a Prometheus /metrics endpoint, also add:\n\n     obs.scrape: \"true\"\n     obs.scrape.port: \"<port>\"    # port that serves /metrics (e.g. \"8080\")\n     obs.scrape.path: \"/metrics\" # omit if the path is already /metrics\n\n4. To send traces and structured logs via OpenTelemetry, set these env vars\n   on the service (SDK-agnostic — works with any OTel-instrumented app):\n\n     OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT: \"http://otel-collector:4317\"\n     OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL: \"grpc\"\n     OTEL_SERVICE_NAME: \"<service-name>\"\n     OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES: \"service.namespace=<project-name>\"\n\n5. Do NOT modify the observability stack itself (/opt/observability).\n   Do NOT add Loki, Jaeger, Prometheus, or Grafana to this project's compose file.\n\nAfter making these changes, run `docker compose up -d` in the project directory.\nThe project will appear automatically in the Grafana dashboard at\nhttp://localhost:3003/d/obs-projects within ~30 seconds.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Query observability data from your agent\n\nOnce connected, agents can also query the stack directly via MCP — no need to know the underlying APIs.\n\nAdd to `.mcp.json` in any project:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"observability\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"https://app.example.com/mcp\",\n      \"headers\": { \"Authorization\": \"Bearer __MCP_API_KEY__\" }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n| Tool | What it does |\n|------|--------------|\n| `list_projects` | All observed project namespaces |\n| `get_project_health(project)` | Log count, error rate, trace presence — last 1h |\n| `query_logs(project, search?)` | Search logs with optional text filter |\n| `get_recent_errors(project)` | Recent error/exception/fatal lines |\n| `query_metrics(promql)` | Raw PromQL query against Prometheus |\n| `get_traces(project)` | Recent Jaeger traces for a service |\n| `get_stack_health()` | Health of all 4 stack components |",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Agent Integration Prompt",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": true,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 22 },
      "id": 201,
      "title": "▲ Hide integration prompt",
